Backend Execution Commands
Run these commands from the brightloop/backend directory to initialize the migration environment, generate the unified database schema, and boot the API alongside the billing worker:   DOS:: 1. Initialize Alembic (if not already done)
alembic init alembic

:: 2. Generate the initial migration containing all tables
alembic revision --autogenerate -m "Initial schema: Identity, Catalog, Subscriptions, Billing, Peers"

:: 3. Apply the migration to the PostgreSQL database
alembic upgrade head

:: 4. Start the FastAPI API server
uvicorn app.main:app --reload --port 8000


:: 1. Run the seed script to populate the database and enqueue the job
python scripts/seed_database.py

:: 2. Test the API (In a new terminal, using curl or your browser)
curl http://localhost:8000/api/v1/catalog/plans
curl http://localhost:8000/api/v1/analytics/revenue

:: 3. Run the billing worker manually to observe the FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED transaction
cd backend
python -m app.workers.billing_worker